# Commit as you go

When you change this project, commit as soon as a coherent unit of work is done. Do not wait for a separate request to commit.

- Commit after the change is complete and checked (tests, lint, or the relevant verification).
- Prefer small commits that each do one thing over one large commit at the end.
- Write a concise message that says why the change was made.
- Follow the git safety protocol: no force push, no skipped hooks, no git config changes, and no secrets.
- Push only when asked.
